// Phase 6.5b-2. The integration behavior projection.
//
// WHAT IS ABSENT IS THE POINT. There is no `use create`, no `use update`, no
// `use delete`, no `use association _Items` and not one buyer action: no
// submit, approve, reject, cancel or removeItem, and neither sendToSupplier nor
// recordDeliveryResult, which belong to the outbound coordinator and to nobody
// else. An integration client gets exactly one verb.
//
// NO `use draft;`, deliberately. ZJP_I_PurchaseOrder is draft-enabled for the
// buyer UI, but a projection is free to expose the active instances only, and
// Cloud Integration has no business reaching a buyer's unsaved draft. The
// action carries its own draft guard as well, so this is defence in depth
// rather than the only lock - but the surface should not offer the door at all.
projection;

strict ( 2 );

define behavior for ZJP_API_PurchaseOrder
{
  // The whole API. Authorization delegates to the root's update authorization,
  // as declared on the base behavior definition.
  use action applySupplierResponse;
}
